hooded:
I dissect the play;
Seems it, to my hooded thinking,
Reflex holiday.

hooked:
With grimy fingers clutching and crooked,
Tight skin, a nose all bony and hooked,
And a shaking, sharp, suspicious way;

hooves:
broken by your feet;
your horse’s hooves
tread softer than a deer’s;

hooting:
Complaining all the while
In horrid, hooting stanza;
Then chase itself down hill

hooks:
I kept its pauses, marked its emphasis;
My voice, empaled upon rhyme’s golden hooks,
Not once would writhe, nor quiver, nor revolt;

hoof:
The pitying rain began to fall;
I lay and heard each pattering hoof
Upon my lowly, thatched roof,

hookey's:
Mus' feel mussiful.
Hookey's wrong, I know it
Ain't no gent'man's trick;
